# Kernel tarball hash for the pinned BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_VERSION_VALUE.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Buildroot resolves the kernel's hash file to `linux/linux.hash` (see
# LINUX_HASH_FILES / pkg-patch-hash-dirs in package/pkg-utils.mk:163) --
# a path that DOES NOT EXIST in the release. Its actual hashes live in
# linux/from-6.17/linux.hash, which that lookup never consults. The result is
# that a pinned custom kernel version downloads with only
#   "WARNING: no hash file for linux-<ver>.tar.xz"
# and is NEVER VERIFIED -- and BR2_DOWNLOAD_FORCE_CHECK_HASHES does not save
# you, because it can only force the checking of hashes that exist.
#
# That silently defeats G5 (pinned kernel + hash). pkg-patch-hash-dirs also
# searches $(BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR)/<pkg>/, which is why this file is here and
# why the defconfig sets BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR.
#
# Deliberately no Buildroot version in the paragraph above: it describes a
# MECHANISM, and naming the version it was first observed on makes the note
# read as stale the moment the pin moves, even when nothing changed. Re-verified
# against the pinned tree on 2026-07-25 (Buildroot 2026.05.1): `linux/linux.hash`
# still does not exist, the real hashes are still under linux/from-6.17/ and
# linux/before-6.17/, and pkg-patch-hash-dirs is still package/pkg-utils.mk:163.
# RE-VERIFY ON A BUILDROOT BUMP -- if upstream ever ships linux/linux.hash, this
# whole file becomes redundant rather than load-bearing.
#
# WHERE THIS HASH COMES FROM -- read before changing it.
# Transcribed from kernel.org's PGP-signed release manifest:
#
#     https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/sha256sums.asc
#
# That signed file is the ONLY source of truth. Do NOT produce this value by
# downloading the tarball and running sha256sum on it -- that is circular and
# certifies nothing. Independently corroborated against Buildroot's own
# linux/from-6.17/linux.hash, which agrees byte-for-byte.
#
# A kernel bump (manual, or Renovate under P4.7) MUST update this line from the
# signed manifest for the new version, or the build will fail closed -- which is
# the intended behaviour.
sha256  3712fc1ec839e4daac981176c8518912e8f452650aaedfe4381da4419613a431  linux-6.18.40.tar.xz

# WHERE THE 7.2-rc4 HASH COMES FROM -- weaker provenance, stated honestly.
# kernel.org publishes NO signed manifest for -rc kernels: sha256sums.asc
# covers releases only, and linux/linux.mk fetches "-rc" versions as
# cgit-generated snapshots from https://git.kernel.org/torvalds/t/ (hence
# .tar.gz, not .tar.xz). Upstream Buildroot handles that by exempting the file
# via BR_NO_CHECK_HASH_FOR -- but BR2_DOWNLOAD_FORCE_CHECK_HASHES (kept, per
# G5) EMPTIES that exemption list (package/pkg-download.mk:119), so without a
# line here every RT variant build fails closed at the kernel download with
# "No hash found for linux-7.2-rc4.tar.gz".
#
# This value is therefore transcribed from a verified local download
# (2026-07-20: 265,644,370 bytes; the tarball extracted cleanly and its
# top-level Makefile reads VERSION=7 PATCHLEVEL=2 EXTRAVERSION=-rc4) -- the
# circularity the release-hash rule above forbids, accepted here because no
# signed source exists to transcribe from. It still buys TOFU pinning: every
# later download must be byte-identical to the inspected one. ACCEPTED RISK:
# cgit regenerating the snapshot with different compression bytes would fail
# this check spuriously -- that failure is closed, not open, and an -rc pin is
# short-lived by nature (the next version bump replaces this line anyway).
#
# Weak corroboration, worth exactly what it is: the rc4 snapshot CI fetched on
# the Renovate bump PR (run 29751573822, before it failed closed here for want
# of this line) was 265,644,370 bytes -- byte-count-identical to the local
# download this hash was taken from. Two fetches from different hosts at
# different times agreeing on length is NOT a signature, and does not upgrade
# TOFU to verified provenance; it only rules out a truncated or mid-flight
# corrupted local copy, which is the one failure this pin could otherwise bless.
sha256  0b97442738ce5485694f7d9734cac94bee01839fe0d5635cbf18df30144ebcfc  linux-7.2-rc4.tar.gz
